docs {
  # Resolve Transfer Account

  Use this endpoint before sending money to a Nigerian bank account.

  The frontend sends the selected bank code and account number. The backend uses Paystack privately to fetch the account name.

  ## Endpoint

  `POST /api/v1/wallet/transfers/resolve-account`

  ## Authentication

  Required.

  ```txt
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
  ```

  ## Request Body

  ```json
  {
    "bankCode": "058",
    "accountNumber": "0123456789"
  }
  ```

  ## Important

  `bankCode` must be the Paystack bank code for account-name lookup.

  Maplerad bank codes are different and should be used later when the actual transfer endpoint is implemented.

  ## Success Response

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Account resolved successfully",
    "account": {
      "accountNumber": "0123456789",
      "accountName": "JOHN DOE",
      "bankCode": "058",
      "provider": "paystack"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Frontend Flow

  - user selects bank
  - user enters 10 digit account number
  - call this endpoint
  - show `account.accountName`
  - user confirms and enters PIN
  - backend sends the final transfer through Maplerad later
}
